				1735,
				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Localize IPC dispatch macro and notify Cocoon on Sky saves\n\nMove the `call!` macro definition from the module level into the `mountain_ipc_invoke` function in `WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs` to capture `RunTime` and `ApplicationHandle` via closure hygiene, avoiding external dependencies and enforcing strict scope.\n\nSimplify `TraceStep` in `TraceLog.rs` by removing unnecessary blank lines. Update `CustomEditorProvider`, `TestProvider`, and `StatusBarProvider` to explicitly import `tauri::Manager` alongside `Emitter` for future context access.\n\nEnhance the `proxy_cocoon` utility to map IPC errors to strings for cleaner propagation. In `Workspace.rs`, refactor the Sky save handling to capture the result and immediately notify the Cocoon extension host via `$acceptModelSaved`. This ensures extensions relying on `onDidSaveTextDocument` trigger correctly for saves initiated by the UI layer.",
			"SHA": "56cd4ccb60cd2047bea5f38d2ba58cff67d5e32f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T11:13:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1735,
				8
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Centralize Cocoon IPC calls and unify URI sanitization\n\nReplace verbose inline `SendRequestToSideCar` logic in `CustomEditorProvider`, `StatusBarProvider`, `TestProvider`, `Authentication`, `Task`, and `FileSystem` handlers with the new centralized `proxy_cocoon` helper in `Utilities::Proxy`. This helper abstracts the retrieval of `ApplicationRunTime`, `IPCProvider`, and method string construction, reducing boilerplate across the `CreateEffectForRequest` tree.\n\nConcurrently, extract the `StripFileUriScheme` logic from `FileSystem.rs` into the shared `Utilities::Params` module as `strip_file_uri`. Update all `FileSystem` operations (ReadFile, WriteFile, ReadDirectory, Stat, CreateDirectory, Delete, Rename, Copy) to utilize this unified utility for normalizing `file://` URIs, ensuring consistent path handling for the extension host.\n\nThis consolidation enforces a single source of truth for IPC dispatch and file path normalization, aligning with the project's architectural standardization efforts.",
			"SHA": "a430e1c403378f8fa7723f9842f1cfc23ba04b56"
